1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:27,420
This Match...

3
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:31,260
The winner is the Jianghai Team!

4
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:34,140
That's why I asked him to be your Coach.

5
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:36,450
My judgment's still pretty sharp, isn't it?

6
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:38,940
Coach, why didn't my Grandpa come?

7
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:41,820
It was completely underhanded.
You made me lose so much face.

8
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:44,580
I only did it to help the Chengnan Team take the Title!

9
00:01:45,820 --> 00:01:46,620
You are so presumptuous.

10
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:49,980
It's clear you still aren't ready to
sincerely own up to your mistakes.

11
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:51,420
Coach!

12
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:53,340
Please don't kick Teddy off the Team.

13
00:01:55,040 --> 00:01:56,500
I was the one who put him up to it.

14
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Episode 22

15
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:19,740
Captain!

16
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:28,000
Teddy... this...

17
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:33,000
Captain!

18
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:36,540
I know.

19
00:02:37,180 --> 00:02:39,420
You took all the blame for me.

20
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:43,260
But I'm the one who actually did it.

21
00:02:44,380 --> 00:02:45,660
I figure...

22
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:49,980
if I just stood by and let you take the fall,

23
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:53,340
That wouldn't be right at all.

24
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:54,780
Teddy!

25
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:57,660
Don't let your emotions get the better of you.

26
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:02,460
I know you really want to stay on the Jianghai Team.

27
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:07,990
If you leave and I stay,
I'd never feel right about it.

28
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:14,910
Captain!

29
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:18,300
What time's the earliest bus back to the City?

30
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Teddy,

31
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:23,580
From now on... don't call me Captain anymore.

32
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:27,820
It's a hard habit to break.

33
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:40,860
Are you here to gloat?

34
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:43,260
I hope both of you

35
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,140
will reconsider and stick around.

36
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:49,980
Why are you doing this?

37
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:53,340
I don't think you guys should leave.

38
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:55,740
The Matches ahead are only going to get tougher.

39
00:03:56,100 --> 00:03:59,100
The Jianghai Team can't afford to lose
any more good people to infighting.

40
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:01,980
But Coach, he...

41
00:04:02,140 --> 00:04:04,380
I already made a request to the Coach.

42
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:08,710
Mark, the truth is, we just have different personalities.

43
00:04:10,580 --> 00:04:12,060
After all this time,

44
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:14,460
I think we've come to understand each other a lot better.

45
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:15,900
I think

46
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:18,300
we're gonna get along just fine from now on.

47
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:22,620
But Coach will never forgive us.

48
00:04:22,980 --> 00:04:24,060
Who says he won't?

49
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:36,540
What I wanted was to see you own up to
your mistakes with genuine remorse.

50
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:38,460
Coach, I...

51
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:39,900
Coach!

52
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:43,260
The truth is, I acted on my own when I framed Leo.

53
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:46,620
The Captain really had no idea about any of it.

54
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:50,460
If anyone should be punished, let it be me alone.

55
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:54,300
Punishment was never my goal.

56
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:57,660
What I really wanted was to see you
recognize your mistakes and change.

57
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:00,060
Honestly, I know

58
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,460
that in terms of skill and ability,

59
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:04,380
I can't compare to Leo.

60
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:07,740
I should be working harder to catch up to him.

61
00:05:10,020 --> 00:05:11,100
And another thing.

62
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,500
Leo came knocking on my door

63
00:05:13,960 --> 00:05:16,380
in the middle of the night to plead your case.

64
00:05:17,020 --> 00:05:18,780
Bet you didn't see that one coming.

65
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:22,620
I know I'm partly to blame, too.

66
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:25,000
Maybe it's just my personality.

67
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:26,460
It's what caused all the misunderstandings

68
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:28,150
and made things worse between us.

69
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:29,340
Stop, Leo.

70
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:33,180
It was all my fault.

71
00:05:35,260 --> 00:05:37,500
I was always whispering in the Captain's
ear and stirring the pot.

72
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:41,340
I'm the one who led the Captain astray.

73
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:43,710
I'm sorry.

74
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:44,700
Alright.

75
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:47,550
That kind of self-reflection...

76
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:49,980
now that's what a real Jianghai Team member looks like!

77
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:53,790
So, Coach, does this mean they can stay?

78
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:54,780
I'm sure the Coach will say yes.

79
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:57,660
Last time I messed up, didn't the Coach forgive me, too?

80
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:01,020
Just don't let it happen again.

81
00:06:01,180 --> 00:06:02,860
I promise, I'll never do anything like that again.

82
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:09,660
Coach, even though everyone's forgiven me,

83
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:13,020
I still think that the new Captain

84
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,420
should be Leo.

85
00:06:18,660 --> 00:06:20,220
Yeah, we're all for it!

86
00:06:21,640 --> 00:06:22,620
We support it, too!

87
00:06:22,780 --> 00:06:23,580
I agree.

88
00:06:24,040 --> 00:06:24,540
Coach...

89
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:27,900
Leo.

90
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:30,300
I hope that by taking on the Captain role,

91
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:31,740
you can put your talents to good use

92
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:35,580
and really become a true part of this big Family of ours.

93
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:40,860
Leo!

94
00:06:41,320 --> 00:06:42,400
I'll back you up 100% from now on.

95
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:44,220
I'll give the Training everything I've got.

96
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:46,620
I'll do it all for the Team's honor.

97
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:49,500
I'll never do anything to divide this Team again.

98
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:51,900
Leo, just say yes and be our Captain!

99
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:53,820
Leo, please say yes!

100
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:56,700
Leo!

101
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:07,260
Alright. Since that's how it is,

102
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:08,900
I won't let everyone's faith in me go to waste.

103
00:07:09,640 --> 00:07:11,100
I'll give it everything I've got.

104
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:18,300
With that kind of spirit, the Jianghai Team
has a real shot at greatness!

105
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:45,860
Morning Everyone!

106
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:47,580
Morning, Coach!

107
00:07:48,520 --> 00:07:49,720
I've got an Announcement to make.

108
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:53,310
Our summer break is almost over.

109
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:55,260
And our Training here is about to wrap up, too.

110
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:57,660
You've all finished your Summer homework, right?

111
00:07:58,120 --> 00:07:59,100
Yeah!

112
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:00,540
Alright.

113
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,980
Then I'm announcing that for the next few days,

114
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:05,340
every evening, I'm going to have Shawn

115
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:08,220
hold a Class for all of you.

116
00:08:08,300 --> 00:08:09,300
Huh?

117
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:11,070
Shawn, come on up here

118
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:13,020
and tell everyone what your Teaching Plan is.

119
00:08:13,480 --> 00:08:14,460
Everyone, give him a round of applause!

120
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:21,180
Coach!

121
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:24,060
I didn't think you'd actually taken my suggestion to heart.

122
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:25,980
You were absolutely right.

123
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:28,350
Only by combining theory with hands-on practice

124
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:30,300
can you build a truly solid foundation,

125
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:32,220
and go further in the long run.

126
00:08:32,680 --> 00:08:34,140
How could I not take it seriously? Come on.

127
00:08:35,560 --> 00:08:37,980
Coach, about that Teaching Plan...

128
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:39,900
I didn't actually bring it with me.

129
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:44,700
So maybe we should just change the plan, Coach.

130
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:47,100
Yeah, yeah! We can just use the
time to go over our School work!

131
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:49,980
Or practicing our Signature Moves in the evening works, too!

132
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:51,900
Running laps wouldn't be a problem either!

133
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:56,190
But Coach...

134
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:57,660
I can recite the whole plan from memory!

135
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:02,940
Alright then, let's hear it.

136
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,000
Day 1:

137
00:09:08,680 --> 00:09:11,580
The History and Development of the Yo-Yo, Part 1.

138
00:09:12,020 --> 00:09:13,020
Day 2...

139
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:16,380
The History and Development of the Yo-Yo, Part 2.

140
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:17,820
Day 3...

141
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,730
The History and Development of the Yo-Yo, Part 3.

142
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:23,100
Oh, for crying out loud.

143
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:24,540
Hey, don't be like that.

144
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:26,940
You can't understand the "why" until
you first understand the "what."

145
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:30,300
We need the professional spirit to really
dig deep and get to the bottom of things.

146
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:33,630
That's the only way to ensure our knowledge
develops real depth and complexity,

147
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:37,020
and the only way to push forward into more
advanced, cutting-edge theory.

148
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:39,900
We get it, Professor Shawn.

149
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:42,780
Could you please just hurry up and finish telling us the plan?

150
00:09:43,240 --> 00:09:44,220
Day 4, Evening:

151
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:47,100
An Overview of Basic Yo-Yo Knowledge.

152
00:09:48,040 --> 00:09:49,020
Day 5...

153
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:26,940
And finally...

154
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:30,780
an Introduction and exploration of
advanced, cutting-edge theory.

155
00:10:32,680 --> 00:10:33,630
Can't you just skip ahead?

156
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:36,060
Just tell us the advanced, cutting-edge theory stuff now!

157
00:10:36,520 --> 00:10:38,940
That's way too impatient.

158
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:41,820
You'll never accomplish anything worthwhile
with an attitude like that.

159
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:44,700
Yeah, but by the time you actually get to that part,

160
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:47,580
our Training Camp will practically be over!

161
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:50,940
Alright, I'll make a slight adjustment.

162
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,310
We'll increase the workload for each evening's class.

163
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:59,100
No! Please, no!

164
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:17,820
This is brutal.

165
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:20,700
I'd honestly rather go stand out in the rain

166
00:11:22,780 --> 00:11:24,060
than listen to Shawn

167
00:11:24,220 --> 00:11:25,980
drone on and on about Yo-Yo theory.

168
00:11:26,340 --> 00:11:27,420
Alright, everyone,

169
00:11:27,680 --> 00:11:29,820
do you know which country the Yo-Yo originally came from?

170
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:31,260
China!

171
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:32,190
Yeah.

172
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:33,660
That's something every descendant of China

173
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:35,480
should feel proud of.

174
00:11:37,380 --> 00:11:39,870
He's just guessing wildly.

175
00:11:39,880 --> 00:11:41,790
Mickey, stop goofing around.

176
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:44,700
Does anyone know what the world's oldest toy is?

177
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:46,000
Can anyone tell me?

178
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:47,600
I know, It's a Yo-Yo.

179
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:51,420
Wrong. I'm warning you, Chuck.

180
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:53,820
You won't get far in your studies if you just guess wildly.

181
00:11:55,720 --> 00:11:56,700
Everyone, remember this.

182
00:11:57,160 --> 00:12:00,060
The Yo-Yo is known as the 2nd oldest toy in the world.

183
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:02,940
The very oldest toy is the doll.

184
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:05,720
You really think that's important?

185
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:07,100
Of course it's important!

186
00:12:07,650 --> 00:12:11,100
Any kind of knowledge shouldn't just be deep,
it should be broad, too.

187
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:13,500
A broad knowledge Base

188
00:12:13,760 --> 00:12:15,420
is a key part of building personal character.

189
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:21,180
Please, could you just stop asking questions?

190
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:26,460
From what I can see, you're not exactly
listening all that closely yourself.

191
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:27,900
The problem is,

192
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:29,820
whenever someone provokes him,

193
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:32,220
he just goes on and on forever.

194
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:33,660
At this rate, how long are we gonna have to wait

195
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:36,060
before he finally gets to the
advanced cutting-edge theory?

196
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:40,380
Probably around the day after tomorrow,
in the middle of the night.

197
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:44,700
The Yo-Yo in ancient times...

198
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:48,540
Mickey.

199
00:12:49,180 --> 00:12:50,460
Is Class over?

200
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:59,100
What part are we on now?

201
00:12:59,560 --> 00:13:01,020
We're still on ancient times.

202
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:06,780
In England, the Yo-Yo was known as the "Prince's Treasure."

203
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:10,140
In France, it was known as the "Norman Yo-Yo."

204
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:15,870
Stop poking me all the time.

205
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:16,860
When did I ever poke you?

206
00:13:18,560 --> 00:13:21,180
Shawn, give it back.

207
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:24,540
You can pick it up from Coach Tony tomorrow.

208
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:26,000
What?

209
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:29,340
In the early 18th century,

210
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:32,220
the Yo-Yo was called the "Prince's Treasure" in England.

211
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:36,540
In France, it was popularized under the name "Norman Yo-Yo."

212
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:41,340
It became especially fashionable among the
upper classes in France and England,

213
00:13:42,560 --> 00:13:45,180
and was even introduced to the Prince of Wales in England.

214
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:48,540
It was regarded by the nobility as

215
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,240
a fashionable and noble toy.

216
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:56,670
It could ease the fatigue of deep contemplation

217
00:13:56,680 --> 00:13:57,660
and even help calm

218
00:13:58,020 --> 00:14:00,650
the nerves of those about to face the guillotine.

219
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:02,460
The guillotine?

220
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:04,380
Who talks about guillotines at night?

221
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:06,300
It'll give us nightmares.

222
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:09,180
Who said you could sleep?

223
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:10,300
Oh Chuck,

224
00:14:11,080 --> 00:14:13,980
Turn in a written self-reflection to Coach Tony tomorrow.

225
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:17,820
No, please!

226
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:27,500
Hello?

227
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:29,340
Oh, it's you.

228
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:31,260
I was just looking for you.

229
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,180
I was looking for you, too.

230
00:14:37,180 --> 00:14:37,980
Is something up?

231
00:14:39,300 --> 00:14:40,380
You go first.

232
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:42,270
Alright.

233
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:44,700
Our Training Camp wraps up in a couple days,
and we'll all be heading back.

234
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:46,140
I've booked a bus.

235
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:48,540
I wanted to see if your Chengnan Team
would like to ride back together.

236
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:49,980
Sure!

237
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:52,830
We can split part of the rental fee

238
00:14:52,840 --> 00:14:54,260
so we can both save money.

239
00:14:54,400 --> 00:14:55,400
No need.

240
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:57,660
The bus won't be full with just our Team anyway.

241
00:14:58,120 --> 00:15:00,060
Empty seats are just empty seats.
We might as well bring you along.

242
00:15:00,700 --> 00:15:01,730
We'd feel bad about that.

243
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:04,000
There's nothing to feel bad about.

244
00:15:04,360 --> 00:15:05,340
Besides,

245
00:15:05,500 --> 00:15:06,780
Didn't you cover the full cost

246
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:08,700
of that Exhibition Match for us once?

247
00:15:09,160 --> 00:15:11,100
I've got to return the favor somehow.

248
00:15:14,440 --> 00:15:15,900
Speaking of the exhibition match...

249
00:15:17,020 --> 00:15:18,780
I actually feel a bit embarrassed about it.

250
00:15:19,040 --> 00:15:20,220
What's wrong?

251
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:24,060
That's exactly what I wanted to talk to you about.

252
00:15:24,520 --> 00:15:25,980
My Players actually went behind my back

253
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:29,340
and spied on your Jianghai Team's Signature Moves.

254
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:31,740
I didn't find out about it until after the Match.

255
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:35,440
I've already given them a serious scolding.

256
00:15:36,520 --> 00:15:38,940
I wanted to come and clear the air
with you about this whole thing

257
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:43,740
and apologize to you on their behalf.

258
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:45,180
That won't be necessary.

259
00:15:45,920 --> 00:15:49,500
I already know you had nothing to do with it.

260
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:58,140
Shawn, give me back my "Smiling, Proud Wanderer"!

261
00:15:58,600 --> 00:16:00,540
No. You can get it from Coach Tony tonight.

262
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:03,900
I know you haven't turned it in to him yet.

263
00:16:04,540 --> 00:16:06,780
You can totally make the call yourself. Just give it back.

264
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:08,670
I'm not one to abuse my Authority.

265
00:16:08,680 --> 00:16:11,100
The rules we set are meant to be strictly followed by everyone.

266
00:16:12,040 --> 00:16:13,980
Rules are made by people!

267
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:15,900
Can't you just bend them a little?

268
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:17,820
How can you say something like that?

269
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:21,180
Let me tell you something, I am
absolutely not giving it back to you.

270
00:16:21,640 --> 00:16:22,620
Because...

271
00:16:22,880 --> 00:16:25,500
I have to teach a harsh lesson to someone

272
00:16:25,960 --> 00:16:27,420
who's constantly disrespected theory.

273
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:29,790
And what about you, who's always dismissed practical skill?

274
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:32,190
Maybe I should be teaching you a lesson, too.

275
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,180
I never dismissed practical skill!

276
00:16:33,640 --> 00:16:35,100
I've been exploring it all along.

277
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:37,600
Exploring?

278
00:16:37,960 --> 00:16:40,350
You can't even do 30 basic Yo-Yo moves,

279
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:43,340
and you have the nerve to talk to me about "Exploring"?

280
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:45,660
I'm the type of talent that develops
slowly at first, then explodes.

281
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:49,500
When the critical moment comes, I'll soar to the top.

282
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:53,310
Hmph. Looks to me like you've had
plenty of "slow" and zero "explosion."

283
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:54,750
You'll never get there.

284
00:16:54,760 --> 00:16:55,740
I'm not arguing with you.

285
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:56,800
Anyways,

286
00:16:56,860 --> 00:16:58,620
Theory guides practice. That's just a given.

287
00:16:59,080 --> 00:17:01,020
Wait, I'm done wasting my breath on you.

288
00:17:01,480 --> 00:17:03,870
Either way, I don't accept you teaching us this class.

289
00:17:03,880 --> 00:17:04,860
I'm not having it.

290
00:17:06,080 --> 00:17:08,220
Alright, how about this? Let's have a Match.

291
00:17:09,160 --> 00:17:12,540
If you win, I'll forget about "The Smiling, Proud Wanderer."

292
00:17:13,480 --> 00:17:16,860
But if you lose, not only do you give me back my novel,

293
00:17:17,320 --> 00:17:20,220
you have to buy me a new copy, too. How about that?

294
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:21,660
A Match?

295
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:23,070
That's not fair.

296
00:17:23,080 --> 00:17:25,020
I'm still grinding away at those 30 Basic Moves.

297
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:28,380
Fine. Then we'll stick to competing
with only the Beginner Moves.

298
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:47,100
Even though your Team won the match,

299
00:17:48,040 --> 00:17:50,470
the Chengnan Team is going to double down on our Training.

300
00:17:52,540 --> 00:17:53,820
By the time the Autumn Tournament rolls around,

301
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,700
we'll see who comes out on top.

302
00:17:57,160 --> 00:18:00,060
Alright. You're welcome to challenge us anytime.

303
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,300
But honestly, I don't think we need to be so Competitive.

304
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:04,380
Winning and losing isn't the important thing.

305
00:18:05,320 --> 00:18:06,300
What really matters

306
00:18:06,760 --> 00:18:09,660
is building character and determination in these kids.

307
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:13,980
You really have a knack for mentoring young people.

308
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:16,860
The kids are all really close to you.

309
00:18:17,600 --> 00:18:20,220
Sometimes, I really do think of them as my own children.

310
00:18:20,680 --> 00:18:22,620
Though they can be a real handful, too.

311
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:38,460
So why haven't you put any thought
into your own personal life?

312
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:43,260
Well, that situation hasn't exactly worked
itself out yet. And honestly, I feel like

313
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:45,660
I'm just more at ease

314
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:48,540
when I'm spending time with the kids.

315
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:52,860
Women... they're just too complicated.

316
00:18:55,240 --> 00:18:56,300
What does this have to do with women?

317
00:18:57,820 --> 00:19:00,060
I think you're just way too old-fashioned.

318
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:01,920
You just don't understand how women think.

319
00:19:04,540 --> 00:19:05,820
Well, don't go pointing fingers at me.

320
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:08,700
Aren't you the same way?

321
00:19:11,080 --> 00:19:13,980
Me? I'm a bachelor by choice.

322
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:17,340
Being single is so carefree and relaxing.

323
00:19:18,760 --> 00:19:22,910
Come on, no lies between friends.
Who was it that, right after graduation,

324
00:19:23,080 --> 00:19:25,500
was crying and wailing about
wanting to be someone's bride?

325
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:47,580
I've never actually seen Shawn in a Match before.

326
00:19:48,040 --> 00:19:49,980
This is a once-in-a-lifetime showdown.

327
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:51,420
If Matthew wins,

328
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:53,820
does that mean we don't have to go to class anymore?

329
00:19:54,080 --> 00:19:56,700
Duh. Matthew's got this in the bag for sure.

330
00:19:57,160 --> 00:19:59,580
I can't wait to see the look
on Shawn's face when he loses.

331
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:02,460
Would that mean he's saved all of humanity?

332
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:04,380
He'll have saved the whole universe, at least!

333
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,460
Are you ready yet?

334
00:20:15,400 --> 00:20:17,340
Can't you see I'm doing my warm-up exercises?

335
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:47,070
Ready or not, I'm about to make my move!

336
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:49,980
Hold on, I haven't even drawn my Yo-Yo yet!

337
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Behold

338
00:20:55,240 --> 00:20:57,180
This is my Limited-Edition Yo-Yo:

339
00:20:58,120 --> 00:20:59,100
The Ghost Face.

340
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:03,000
[Name: Shawn] [Team: Jianghai]
[Yo-Yo: Ghost Face] [Special Move: Phantom Swap]

341
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:05,310
Ghost Face, Human Face...

342
00:21:05,320 --> 00:21:06,750
doesn't matter what Yo-Yo you use. Here I go!

343
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:08,000
Wait!

344
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,100
Hey, you haven't announced the name of your Yo-Yo yet!

345
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:12,540
Who said I had to announce its name?

346
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:14,940
I think it adds a sense of proper ceremony.

347
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:16,350
A Match should have

348
00:21:16,360 --> 00:21:18,270
a dignified procedure, okay?

349
00:21:18,280 --> 00:21:19,230
Fine, fine.

350
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:20,700
My Yo-Yo's name is Shockwave. Here I go!

351
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:22,620
Wait, hold on!

